  - Vue
  - Vanilla JavaScript

  3. Flexible Usage Patterns

  // Standalone API
  const doc = new TOMDocument();
  const button = new TOMButton();
  button.addEventListener('click', handler);

  // Framework integration
  <TOMButton onClick={handler}>Click me</TOMButton>

  4. Modular Architecture

  - Core TOM functionality is independent
  - Framework renderers are optional adapters
  - Component library works with any renderer

  Benefits of This Approach:

  ✅ More adoption potential - Not tied to a specific framework✅ Broader use cases - Can integrate into existing projects✅
  Future-proof - Works with new frameworks as they emerge✅ Simpler core - Focus on terminal-specific features✅ Better testing -
  Core functionality isolated from renderer logic

  This makes TOM much more valuable as a foundational library that others can build upon, rather than being limited to one
  specific use case! 🎯


